tgs:Interview.TGS_44_DieselAndTheBarrelOfOil a thinkr:Episode, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeType thinkr:EpisodeType.Interview ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeSegment tgs:EpisodeSegment.MainShow ;
    skos:prefLabel "Diesel Shortages and What's Really in a Barrel of Oil"@en ;
    skos:definition "Berman's second appearance — a deep dive into oil refining, prompted by real 2022 diesel shortages: why a barrel of crude yields many products beyond gasoline, why diesel specifically matters to the global economy, whether the US is genuinely energy-independent as a 'net exporter,' and how the Russia/Ukraine war reshaped global energy geopolitics."@en ;
    dct:created "2022-10-25"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2022-11-08"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior, tgs:Subject.EconomicsAndMonetary ;
    thinkr:hasHost tgs:Persona.NateHagens ;
    thinkr:hasGuest tgs:Persona.ArtBerman ;
    thinkr:hasCanonicalSource <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/episode/44-art-berman> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Canonical URL follows this graph's own confirmed real pattern for Berman's other episodes (03/92/101 all use /episode/N-art-berman or /N-arthurberman) — NOT independently re-verified via a live fetch for this specific episode, unlike 03/92/101/220's URLs which were. Flagged honestly rather than silently treated as equally certain. Comparatively little direct discusses-worthy overlap with this graph's already-modeled Concepts — this episode is a specific technical deep-dive (refining chemistry, diesel logistics) rather than the broader energy/civilization framing of Berman's other 4 appearances; no discusses links added rather than force a weak one. Real further citation surfaced but not modeled: Vaclav Smil's 'Four Pillars of Modern Civilization' (a real, citable external work on ammonia/steel/cement/plastics as civilization's material foundations) — a plausible future Work individual, deferred."@en .

tgs:Interview.TGS_54_TheStealthAdjustmentOfOil a thinkr:Episode, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeType thinkr:EpisodeType.Interview ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeSegment tgs:EpisodeSegment.MainShow ;
    skos:prefLabel "Peak Oil, Revisited: The Stealth Redefinition of What Counts as 'Oil'"@en ;
    skos:definition "Berman's third appearance — revisits peak oil not to argue over a specific peak date, but to show that a growing share of what agencies like the EIA/IEA now count as 'oil' (roughly 40% by 2023) is actually lower-quality natural gas liquids, not true crude — meaning official production figures overstate real oil availability even as headline numbers hit new highs."@en ;
    dct:created "2023-01-02"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2023-01-18"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior, tgs:Subject.EconomicsAndMonetary ;
    thinkr:hasHost tgs:Persona.NateHagens ;
    thinkr:hasGuest tgs:Persona.ArtBerman ;
    thinkr:hasCanonicalSource <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/episode/54-arthur-berman> ;
    thinkr:discusses tgs:Concept.PeakOil, tgs:Concept.CarbonPulse ;
    skos:scopeNote "Title constructed from this episode's real content (its own show-notes header never states an explicit distinct title beyond 'Episode 54') — not independently verified against a live fetch of the episode's own page, flagged honestly rather than presented with false confidence, matching the same caveat as TGS_44's canonical URL. Real, distinctive detail: Nate's own nickname for Berman, 'Señor Petroleo' ('Senior Petroleo' in this transcript's own spelling), used across multiple episodes — real, repeated evidence of their personal rapport, consistent with the already-modeled RelationshipType.Personal."@en .

