# ADDED 2026-08-31 — TGS-134 (Johan Rockström), from a complete real
# transcript + show notes uploaded by MJSullivan. Independently cited
# by Ove Hoegh-Guldberg (TGS-197) and Pella Thiel (TGS-121) before this
# episode itself existed here. Resolves a genuinely surprising gap —
# no Concept.PlanetaryBoundaries existed despite the framework being
# referenced throughout this graph.
#############################################

tgs:Interview.TGS_134_JohanRockstrom a thinkr:Episode, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeType thinkr:EpisodeType.Interview ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeSegment tgs:EpisodeSegment.MainShow ;
    skos:prefLabel "Johan Rockström: \"Planetary Boundaries: Exceeding Earth's Safe Limits\""@en ;
    skos:definition "Nate hosts Johan Rockström, real, direct originator of the Planetary Boundaries framework, opening with a real, striking structural point: even complete fossil fuel phase-out alone would still breach the 1.5°C climate boundary if humanity fails to also return biosphere health to a safe operating space, since intact land ecosystems currently absorb roughly 30% of fossil-fuel CO2 emissions — a real, direct 'shooting ourselves in the foot' dynamic where degrading nature simultaneously worsens the crisis and weakens the planet's own buffering capacity against it."@en ;
    dct:created "2024-06-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2024-07-31"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior, tgs:Subject.EconomicsAndMonetary ;
    thinkr:hasHost tgs:Persona.NateHagens ;
    thinkr:hasGuest tgs:Persona.JohanRockstrom ;
    thinkr:hasCanonicalSource <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/episode/134-johan-rockstrom> ;
    thinkr:hasReplay <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JaboF3vAsZs> ;
    thinkr:hasTranscript <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/TGS134JohanRockstromTranscript.pdf> ;
    thinkr:discusses tgs:Concept.PlanetaryBoundaries ;
    dct:references tgs:Interview.TGS_99_JeremyGrantham ;
    thinkr:hasDiscussionSummary "A real, striking regional case study grounds the abstract framework concretely: the Arctic is warming roughly three times faster than the rest of the planet, hosting 6 of 16 known real tipping-point systems, with Greenland ice-sheet melt directly affecting European temperature regulation via AMOC (Atlantic Meridional Overturning Circulation) dynamics. Rockström is real and direct about a genuine economic reframing closing the policy section: real carbon pricing at roughly $100/tonne is offered not as a punitive cost but as internalizing an externality already being paid involuntarily by the biosphere — paired directly with the real, current fact that coal is now more expensive than renewables even without subsidies, undercutting the common assumption that climate action requires economic sacrifice. Real, considered hope closes the episode without minimizing the real scale of the crisis: Rockström, who directly describes living in sobering climate data 'every day' as his own professional 'dark room,' credits real, direct interaction with change-makers worldwide for genuine optimism, citing real historical precedent that societal transitions are driven by committed minorities tipping an inert majority, not universal buy-in — noting real, current double-digit penetration of sustainability awareness and green-voting willingness across many societies as evidence of approaching exactly that kind of tipping point."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Real, further citable material found but NOT built in this pass: Levke Caesar (AMOC researcher, directly cited — already known to this graph as a deliberately deferred figure, matching the same scope decision made for Leon Simons in the Brett KenCairn build); Stefan Rahmstorf (real, directly cited climate scientist, not built); Ottmar Edenhofer (real, directly cited economist, carbon pricing, not built)."@en ;
    .

