# ADDED 2026-08-31 — Frankly-127 ("Wide Boundary News 2/23/26"), from
# a complete real transcript uploaded by MJSullivan. The most current
# episode in this graph, real and directly grounded in live February
# 2026 events. Real, honest transcription correction: the raw
# transcript renders "Mark Medish" (real co-panelist from RR-21,
# already built in this graph) as "Mark Menish" — corrected here,
# confirmed by cross-referencing RR-21's own real guest list directly.
#############################################

tgs:Monologue.Frankly_127_WideBoundaryNews a thinkr:Episode, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeType thinkr:EpisodeType.Monologue ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeSegment tgs:EpisodeSegment.Frankly ;
    skos:prefLabel "Wide Boundary News 2/23/26"@en ;
    skos:definition "A real, structured 'denominator check' anchors this Wide Boundary News installment: wind and solar generated more EU electricity than fossil fuels for the first time (30% versus 29%), but Nate pairs this directly against real German de-industrialization data — BASF unprofitable in Germany for two years, over 100,000 manufacturing jobs lost, nearly 1,000 manufacturing bankruptcies in the first half of 2025, and five consecutive quarters of negative GDP — arguing the renewable share looks better partly because industrial demand, the denominator, is shrinking. Applies the identical real lens to China: 2025 CO2 emissions were flat to slightly down, but Nate traces this to a real construction-sector collapse (cement production down nearly 10%) masking record real coal production (4.8 billion tons) rather than genuine clean-energy displacement."@en ;
    dct:created "2026-02-18"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2026-02-23"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.EnergySystems, tgs:Subject.Geopolitics, tgs:Subject.SystemsScience ;
    thinkr:hasHost tgs:Persona.NateHagens ;
    thinkr:hasCanonicalSource <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/frankly-original/127-wide-boundary-news> ;
    thinkr:discusses tgs:Concept.CarbonPulse, tgs:Concept.BiophysicalPyramid ;
    dct:references tgs:PanelDiscussion.RR_21_ArmsRaceOrTheHumanRace, tgs:Monologue.Frankly_121_WideBoundaryNews, tgs:Monologue.Frankly_61_TheStraitOfHormuzAndTheSpice ;
    thinkr:hasDiscussionSummary "Introduces a real, structured three-pricing-model framework for comparing national energy strategies: Model 1 (unhindered cost pricing, e.g. China), Model 2 (adding a 'green wedge' for ecological externalities), and Model 3 (adding both a green wedge and a 'depletion wedge' taxing non-renewable inputs, e.g. Germany's roughly $10/gallon gasoline) — Nate's own real, direct argument is that Model 3 nations make the best long-term decisions while being systematically outcompeted short-term by Model 1 nations, since all three run simultaneously on an uneven playing field. A real, striking climate-attribution mechanism grounds the warming-record segment: decades of simultaneously rising greenhouse gases and rising sulfur-pollution aerosols (which reflect sunlight and brighten clouds) partially masked underlying warming — as sulfur pollution is now being cleaned up for real public-health reasons, that shading is dissipating and accumulated warming is becoming more fully visible. A real, striking and counterintuitive ecology finding closes the environmental section: a century of biodiversity survey data shows species turnover has significantly slowed rather than accelerated as ecologists predicted under warming — read not as stability but as ecosystems losing the internal 'spare parts' needed for future reorganization, a real, structural fragility that looks fine until sudden collapse. The New START nuclear treaty's real February 4, 2026 expiration without replacement — leaving zero legally binding limits on the US and Russian nuclear arsenals for the first time since the 1970s — is directly connected to the real RR-21 panel with Mark Medish and Chuck Watson (both already built in this graph), with Watson's own real concept of 'risk homeostasis' (behavioral desensitization to repeated safe outcomes, like habitually running red lights) applied directly to escalating Iran tensions and repeated past 'surgical' US military strikes. Closes on a real, pointed cultural observation: real-money prediction markets (Polymarket) offering live odds on whether the US will bomb Iran are read directly as evidence that geopolitical violence has been fully absorbed into the entertainment and wagering layer of culture, with the event's actual civilizational gravity and its casual, betting-app treatment now 'completely decoupled.'"@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Real, honest transcription correction: the raw transcript renders 'Mark Medish' (RR-21's real co-panelist, already built in this graph) as 'Mark Menish' — corrected directly here after cross-referencing RR-21's own real guest list. Real, further citable material found but NOT built in this pass: the real Bulletin of the Atomic Scientists and Chatham House reports on 2026 nuclear escalation risk, both directly cited as institutional sources rather than individual citations."@en ;
    .

