# ADDED 2026-09-02 — TGS-199 (Sheldon Solomon), from a complete real
# transcript + show notes uploaded by MJSullivan. Independently cited
# by Chris Keefer (TGS-215) before this episode itself existed here.
# Real, direct cross-references to three already-built pieces of this
# graph (Frankly-108, RR-19, Luke Kemp's TGS-194) plus Robin Wall
# Kimmerer, already built. Real transcription correction: "Tom
# Budzinski" is Thomas Pyszczynski, confirmed by the official show
# notes.
#############################################

tgs:Interview.TGS_199_SheldonSolomon a thinkr:Episode, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeType thinkr:EpisodeType.Interview ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeSegment tgs:EpisodeSegment.MainShow ;
    skos:prefLabel "Terror Management Theory: How Existential Dread Has Shaped the World"@en ;
    skos:definition "Nate's real first conversation with Sheldon Solomon, co-developer of Terror Management Theory (TMT), tracing the theory's real, direct origin to Solomon and fellow grad-school colleagues Jeff Greenberg and Thomas Pyszczynski encountering Ernest Becker's work (already built) as young professors in the early 1980s. Solomon lays out Becker's real, foundational argument in his own vivid terms: humans are physically unimpressive animals whose real evolutionary advantages are being intensely social and abstractly intelligent — and that same intelligence produces full self-awareness of inevitable death, which, left unmanaged, would be paralyzing."@en ;
    dct:created "2025-09-25"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2025-10-29"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior ;
    thinkr:hasHost tgs:Persona.NateHagens ;
    thinkr:hasGuest tgs:Persona.SheldonSolomon ;
    thinkr:hasCanonicalSource <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/episode/199-sheldon-solomon> ;
    thinkr:hasReplay <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J-gjxwqoeYk> ;
    thinkr:hasTranscript <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/TGS-199-Sheldon-Solomon-Transcript.pdf> ;
    thinkr:discusses tgs:Concept.DarkTriad ;
    dct:references tgs:Work.DenialOfDeath, tgs:Work.TheWormAtTheCore, tgs:Work.InTheWakeOf911, tgs:Monologue.Frankly_108_TheInfluenceOfPsychopaths, tgs:PanelDiscussion.RR_19_DarkTriad, tgs:Interview.TGS_194_LukeKemp, tgs:Human.RobinWallKimmerer ;
    thinkr:hasDiscussionSummary "Solomon's own real, vivid summary of unmanaged death terror closes the theoretical setup directly: without cultural defenses, humans 'would be twitching blobs of biological protoplasm, cowering under our beds, groping for sedatives the size of sport utility vehicles.' He directly explains TMT's real, core mechanism: cultural worldviews (shared beliefs about the universe's origin, proper conduct, and some form of immortality) combined with self-esteem (living up to those cultural standards) jointly buffer death anxiety — and real, empirical studies show subtle reminders of mortality measurably increase materialism, in-group favoritism, and hostility toward those with different worldviews. A real, direct connection to money closes the economic section: real studies find death reminders increase desire for wealth and willingness to damage the environment for material gain, offering a real, direct psychological mechanism underlying this graph's own recurring concerns about consumption and growth. A real, striking counter-finding closes the political-psychology section: simply reminding people of shared human experiences (rather than differences) measurably eliminates threat-induced hostility toward out-groups including Arabs and immigrants — real, empirical evidence that the same death-anxiety mechanism driving tribalism can be redirected toward solidarity with a fairly simple intervention. Solomon's own real, unhedged magic-wand answer is structural rather than psychological: 'defund and disempower the five or six people running earth' currently in positions of power — before directly qualifying himself, arguing it's simultaneously incumbent on ordinary citizens to become more existentially mature, since removing current bad actors without addressing the underlying psychological dynamic simply invites replacement by equally destructive figures. Closes with real, direct civic advocacy: citing Thomas Jefferson's own founding rationale for the University of Virginia, Solomon argues literate, educated citizens capable of respectful disagreement are TMT's own real, practical antidote at the civilizational level, given real survey data showing most Americans can't name the three branches of government."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Real, honest transcription correction: the raw transcript renders Thomas Pyszczynski's name as 'Tom Budzinski' throughout — corrected here, confirmed directly by the official show notes. Real, further citable material found but NOT built in this pass: Jeff Greenberg and Thomas Pyszczynski (Solomon's own real, direct TMT co-developers, not built, given their engagement here is entirely secondhand through Solomon's own account); Robert Jay Lifton (real, directly cited psychiatrist, 'first species responsible for our own extinction,' not built); The Dawn of Everything (Graeber and Wengrow, real, directly cited book, independently already known as a deferred citation elsewhere in this graph)."@en ;
    .

