#############################################

tgs:Interview.TGS_77_KateRaworth a thinkr:Episode, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeType thinkr:EpisodeType.Interview ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeSegment tgs:EpisodeSegment.MainShow ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kate Raworth: \"The Superorganism V. The Doughnut\""@en ;
    skos:definition "Nate's real, direct first conversation with his own real friend Kate Raworth, creator of Doughnut Economics, exploring whether a holistic economic framework respecting both social sufficiency and planetary boundaries can genuinely counter the growth-driven pull of what Nate calls the economic Superorganism. Raworth directly names conventional economics' central failure: treating GDP growth as the primary measure of success has produced real, measurable environmental overshoot while simultaneously failing to meet basic human needs for a large share of the world's population."@en ;
    dct:created "2023-06-14"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2023-06-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.HumanBehavior, tgs:Subject.EconomicsAndMonetary ;
    thinkr:hasHost tgs:Persona.NateHagens ;
    thinkr:hasGuest tgs:Persona.KateRaworth ;
    thinkr:hasCanonicalSource <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/episode/77-kate-raworth> ;
    thinkr:hasReplay <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7h6X7WBANKY> ;
    thinkr:hasTranscript <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/TGS78_KateRaworth.pdf> ;
    thinkr:discusses tgs:Concept.Superorganism, tgs:Concept.PlanetaryBoundaries ;
    dct:references tgs:Interview.TGS_6_HermanDaly, tgs:Interview.TGS_12_DennisMeadows, tgs:PanelDiscussion.RR_3_UnlearningEconomics, tgs:Interview.TGS_100_NateHagens ;
    thinkr:hasDiscussionSummary "Raworth directly critiques the foundational economic assumption of 'homo economicus' — a rational, self-interested individual optimizer — arguing humans are actually among the most social of all mammal species, making the standard supply-and-demand model a genuinely flawed starting assumption baked into conventional economics from its own foundations. Real, concrete municipal examples ground her argument that Doughnut Economics is already moving from theory to practice: Amsterdam's real, direct adoption of circular-economy policy at the city level, and Grenoble, France's own real, similar municipal initiative, both offered as evidence the framework already has genuine institutional traction. She directly credits Elinor Ostrom's real, Nobel Prize-winning work on commons governance as a real, direct rebuttal to the 'tragedy of the commons' framing, arguing Ostrom's own real research documents genuinely successful long-term collective resource management, not inevitable collective failure. A real, vivid analogy grounds her closing 'finance' preview: comparing standard financial return expectations to a squirrel expecting to find 15% more nuts than it buried the previous autumn, directly questioning why compound financial growth is treated as a reasonable baseline expectation rather than a real, structural design choice worth interrogating. She's real and direct that even successful decoupling stories have limits: Norway's real, genuine success scaling electric vehicle adoption has had no measurable impact on the country's own oil production or exports, a real, direct cautionary example against assuming green technology adoption alone resolves extraction-based economics. Her own real, unhedged magic-wand answer closes the episode: helping every person genuinely feel humanity's interdependence with the whole of Earth's living systems, arguing this single shift in felt understanding, more than any specific policy, is the deepest lever for redesigning economic systems around genuine belonging rather than extraction."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Real, valuable finds surfaced directly by Raworth herself for a real, proposed future Reality Roundtable on finance: Steve Keen and Jon Erickson, both already independently flagged as real, deferred citations elsewhere in this graph's own tracking — this episode reconfirms both as genuine, guest-suggested priorities, not just citation-frequency artifacts. Josh Farley (real, directly named alongside them, not previously flagged, not built). Real, further citable material found but NOT built in this pass: Donella Meadows (real, directly cited, Thinking in Systems, not built); Marjorie Kelly (real, directly cited, regenerative ownership, not built)."@en ;
    .

