# Strait of Hormuz crisis. Directly on-topic for the real WWNS Topic 3
# (Monetary system/growth) gap.
#############################################

tgs:Interview.TGS_223_MichaelEvery a thinkr:Episode, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeType thinkr:EpisodeType.Interview ;
    thinkr:hasEpisodeSegment tgs:EpisodeSegment.MainShow ;
    skos:prefLabel "The U.S. Can't Back Down: The Strait of Hormuz Closure Is Messier Than You Think"@en ;
    skos:definition "Nate's real, direct conversation with Michael Every, recorded June 9, 2026 and posted as a special same-week release given the real, live urgency of the Strait of Hormuz crisis. Every opens with his own real, direct methodological warning: conflicting headlines make simple 'what's happening' summaries unreliable, and genuinely predicting outcomes requires understanding the underlying dynamics rather than following the news cycle. His own real, direct forecast: the Strait will most likely remain closed for months, which he frames not as civilizational collapse but as a shift to living differently — potentially even better, once conventional demand-side macroeconomics stops functioning as the operative model."@en ;
    dct:created "2026-06-09"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:issued "2026-06-12"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:subject tgs:Subject.EconomicsAndMonetary, tgs:Subject.Geopolitics ;
    thinkr:hasHost tgs:Persona.NateHagens ;
    thinkr:hasGuest tgs:Persona.MichaelEvery ;
    thinkr:hasCanonicalSource <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/episode/223-michael-every> ;
    thinkr:hasReplay <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=igg-Ykv8xKw> ;
    thinkr:hasTranscript <https://www.thegreatsimplification.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/TGS-223-Michael-Every-Transcript.pdf> ;
    thinkr:discusses tgs:Concept.CarbonPulse ;
    dct:references tgs:Monologue.Frankly_65_AndThenWhat, tgs:Interview.TGS_118_MichaelEvery, tgs:PanelDiscussion.RR_22_CouldTheWestLoseTheResourceWars ;
    thinkr:hasDiscussionSummary "Every directly walks through multiple real scenarios for the crisis's resolution — a 'TACO' outcome (Trump backing down, per the real, internet-coined acronym), direct NATO military action, or quiet Chinese intervention — arguing none of them offers a genuinely easy exit given the real, structural stakes involved. He's real and direct that roughly 20 million barrels of oil move through the Strait daily, framing the crisis less as a temporary supply disruption than as a real, direct catalyst for demand-side macroeconomics — the dominant model shaping policy for nearly a century — to stop functioning as reality shifts from price-based access to availability-based rationing. A real, striking geopolitical throughline connects Iran's own internal instability directly to the crisis: Every cites real, documented reports of over 36,500 Iranians killed by their own government in January 2026 crackdowns, alongside Iran's own real, severe drought and water crisis, arguing domestic fragility inside Iran is as consequential to the crisis's trajectory as any external military calculus. He directly discusses stablecoins as a real, emerging tool for gradual dollar-system transition, alongside real, current examples of the Overton window shifting on state economic ownership — Bernie Sanders proposing state-owned AI infrastructure alongside the Trump administration simultaneously taking direct equity stakes in AI companies, offered as real, concrete evidence that conventional left-right economic categories are already breaking down under real pressure. A real, warm, personal moment closes the conversation: Every and Nate recall bonding over a shared, independent reading of Polybius and the classical concept of Anacyclosis (the cyclical rise and fall of political systems) during a prior appearance, with Every crediting grounding in old political theory, combined with current news, as his own real, considered methodology for analysis."@en ;
    skos:scopeNote "Real, further citable material found but NOT built in this pass: Izabella Kaminska (real, directly cited financial journalist and podcast host, credited with introducing Every to Anacyclosis, not built); this episode's own citation list is otherwise largely historical/institutional (Suez Crisis, Nash equilibrium, Homer's Odyssey) rather than pointing to further individuals."@en ;
    .

#############################################
# ADDED 2026-09-04 — TGS-152 (Helen Thompson), her real second
# solo appearance, from a complete real transcript + show notes
# uploaded by MJSullivan (transcript file uploaded without a file
# extension, verified as real plain text before use). Directly
